p firmly finally cut each roll  into four even pieces now let's put your  chopsticks skill into test eat this  sandwich sushi rolls with chopsticks  instead so what I love about this is  that because you're taking smaller bites  it makes you think and feel like you're  eating more I'll pack them with the  extra chopped up vegetable sticks soft  with quarter cup of ranch dip from the  previous recipe they are so fun to look  at and eat your friends would definitely  want to steal some let me know in the  comments below and finally egg muffins  for lunch I have previously shed this  recipe in my make-ahead breakfast video  but these egg muffins are also great as  a lunch to go they are high in protein  packed with vegetables and so convenient  to eat what you'll need are four large  eggs 1/2 a cup of mushrooms finely diced  1/2 a cup of carrots finely diced cut a  cup of whole Khans could cut a cup of  cherry tomatoes 1/2 cut a cup of bell  pepper finely diced 1 TSP of olive oil 1  tablespoon of grated cheese and salt and  pepper to taste  previous the oven to 180 degrees Celsius  or 350 degrees Fahrenheit in a large  bowl combine in mushrooms carrots cones  cherry tomatoes bell pepper with olive  oil mix well equally distribute the  vegetable mixture into each muffin  cavity and set aside crack four eggs  into a bowl and lightly beat with a  whisk add salt and pepper  taste and whisk to combine pour the  beaten egg equally into each cavity top  with a little bit of grated cheese then  bake in the oven for 20 minutes or until  muffins are set eggs are cooked through  and unlikely golden allow the muffins to  cool down for about 10 minutes  I'll pack three mushroom egg muffins  into my lunchbox with 1 cup of fruit  mixture and quarter cup of Greek yogurt  this egg muffins are so delicious and  each one is only seventy eight point  five calories you have to try them all  these recipes can be eaten both warm and  chilled they can be stored in the fridge  for up to three 